# Off The Pace - app build/runtime env. Copy to .env.local and fill in to enable. All optional:
# with none set, the app runs exactly as before and all telemetry stays OFF.

# ── Data plane ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override the GCS CDN base. "" = same-origin (offline dev against local app/public/data).
# VITE_DATA_BASE=

# ── Error tracking + RUM (Phase 3) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry DSN. Error tracking AND Core Web Vitals stay entirely off until this is set.
# Works with Sentry.io or a self-hosted Sentry/GlitchTip instance.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# VITE_SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0
# VITE_APP_RELEASE=                 # e.g. the release tag; ties errors to a source-map upload

# Optional privacy-respecting RUM beacon (JSON via navigator.sendBeacon). Web Vitals + app
# timings (duckdb_init, first_query, onnx_warmup) are POSTed here. Independent of Sentry.
# VITE_RUM_ENDPOINT=
# VITE_RUM_SAMPLE_RATE=1

# ── Build-time only: Sentry source-map upload (NOT committed; set in the deploy job) ────────
# When all three are present at build time, vite.config.ts enables @sentry/vite-plugin to upload
# hidden source maps (then deletes them from dist/ so they're never served publicly).
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
